WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.777
A recursive CTE has two parts.

00:00:02.777 --> 00:00:05.312
The anchor term starts the result.

00:00:05.312 --> 00:00:10.212
The recursive term refers to the CTE and finds the next level.

00:00:10.212 --> 00:00:13.137
UNION ALL combines the rows.

00:00:13.137 --> 00:00:18.367
The process continues until the recursive term produces no more matching rows.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:22.342
This is useful for hierarchies and parent-child structures.

00:00:22.342 --> 00:00:28.927
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:36.762
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:45.262
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
